{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Common Markdown emphasis or HTML entities can cause private evidence to appear in the reviewer’s change view."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A public acceptance row can expose short private evidence repeated from an unrecognized verifier row."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Clipping a public report cell can expose the beginning of a longer private quotation by preventing a full match."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Escaping a pipe in a public table cell prevents matching and exposes the copied private evidence."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A Markdown blockquote wrapped mid-word can expose a readable private quotation because the quote prefix interrupts matching."},{"id":"F6","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Short private verifier notes can appear in report prose because the notes are omitted from the prose catalogue."},{"id":"F7","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"When no holdout scenarios exist, private verifier observations are skipped and their quotations can appear in the change view."},{"id":"F8","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Generic success wording shared with private evidence can hide public acceptance evidence or status that a reviewer needs to assess the change."},{"id":"F9","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"normal","reason":"The manifest is appended to published reports and squash messages as extra metadata that contains no plaintext private evidence."}]}